Hi, 
this is my first ascension so I thought it properly to
announce it to the world

As I have been playing at the dtype server the first announcement
got there. This is just a little rewrite of that one.
As far as I know the game has been recorded there for future
playback - so if you really want to you can have a look (as soon
as the mighty dtype gets that playback feature programmed everybody
is looking forward too)
But probably nobody wants to see me sacrifice for 10000 moves before 
finally getting Stormbringer! (Seriously! For a lot of the time it was 
one of the most boring games I have been playing so far. Or is this just 
a shift in perspective which comes with experience? I hope not!)

WARNING: Lots of spoiled things from this point on! WARNING
DO NOT READ if you would like to find things out by yourself
(but then you probably would not be reading RGRN anyways ;-)

Maybe some experiences with my almost-ascensions first and why they
have not worked out: 
I have been playing nethack for about two years now, at first rather
"just like this". Have been getting seriously involved the last couple 
of weeks only (while writing on my diploma thesis). Wished to get it 
done over with finally. So i would not have to play this game all the 
time (grin) and could get on with the rest of my life ;-)
(btw the thesis sucks and I might have to write another one)
So I read almost all the spoilers :-( but still had to find some
things out that nobody ever bothered to tell you... or let's say,
that only show up in the fine print...

I have been past the Castle only five times so far (two before playing
on this server). The first time I ended up fighting three demons at the 
same time in Gehennom. The first one took too long to kill, he called on 
his buddy, and so on... too bad.
The next time I was going to use that c corpse. Not a good idea to
go downstairs then while burdened... (when does anybody write a good
*cockatrice spoiler*? they still scare me!) The next time I was so 
excited (and naive) that I went straight up to the Wizard. I even forgot 
to visit Vlad before and also had to search for the square afterwards. 
No surprise I got killed 7 times (man, had I amulets of lifesaving!) before
Wizard number 11 got me. I had only about 180 hp btw.
So when I started playing on this wonderful server two weeks ago just 
for a change (in fact, I have never got nethack running on my linux box, 
so I kept a copy of windows on this machine just for playing and got bored 
of rebooting all the time!) I was careful to get some hp. Especially after 
I had a closer look at the highscore list. But how? 
I must have overlooked something in the spoilers. I finally found the 
Succubus and Incubus spoiler which gave me some hints.
The potion spoiler proved helpful too. I never imagined it would be so
important! So this time I went with 513hp and something really bad
happened on the Plane of Fire. I am still not sure exactly what, but it
was like this: The Invisible Archon there was stunning me all the time 
from a distance and calling in hordes of monsters. Okay, I thought, let's 
use that ring of conflict only to realize it had gone. I don't know how 
that could have happened. Does Rodney steal rings??? 
So I tried teleporting the nasties away, getting in close enough to kill 
the Archon himself, but to no avail. Then I started running towards the
portal. There were a lot of monsters on the level by then. The Archon 
called them in all the time. There were even four more archons there by 
now... maybe still I would have made it. But then a horned devil got hold 
of my Magicbane with his bullwhip. Snatched it out of my grip just like 
that. And I had no holy water left! And no more wishes (spent them all 
before, which turned out to be a *really bad idea*) and also I had c 
genocided because of my bad experiences with them. Probably also a
*stupid* thing to do. So my unicorn horn went. I burned three Amulets of
Lifesaving and about two steps away from the portal they got me...
Damn. And that was on the day I took my thesis down to the board
of examiners. Bad, bad sign!

But I knew: I just had to come up with an Ascension soon!
And I had lots of freetime now.

So now: the Story of My Succesful Attempt

(Unfortunately I do not keep notes. So I am not always sure about
the right order of events and there might be some lapses. And of course
I won't tell you most of the more boring things)

My priestess found speed boots on Lvl 2. That was a very good sign
I thought! On Lvl 5 I had the feeling it might be a bones from one
of my former games with a leocrotta lurking around somewhere.
(it later turned out i was wrong about the leocrotta, it was killer bees, 
but playing it careful always is a good idea)
So the Mines went first. As soon as I entered them I also had the feeling
it was a bones (turned out to be wrong, I think), so I ran for the downstairs. 
Minetown was a bones too. It was from my own game just before 
where I died when I was accidentally, blindly touching the Priestess in 
my co-aligned temple. Hey, I didn't mean too! (And did not know she would
be that upset. Talk about women ;-)) Well, at least it was a funny death.
So when I realized that, I was quite careful. But this time my priestess
character was aligned to Susanowo instead of Set, so I had a most heartily 
reception in the temple! Seems to be a peculiarity with priests and their
pantheon.
Anyways, I had my first visit of soldier ants there. Usually they're a 
killer for my weak characters. But this time I could jump out of the 
temple, kill one, jump inside and make funny faces to them without them 
coming in while healing myself. This way I spent some thousands moves 
offering. To no avail. Eventually I got the idea that you might not get 
any gifts from your god when offering at an altar with a priest!? So I left 
and took on the main dungeon. Lvl 5 was a bones by McGroat with a dog 
called Sirius. I killed him quickly because I had no food left, sorry,
and I prefer being alone (using Stormbringer a lot).
The killer bees were no problem by then. But the corpse had nothing
exciting about it.
Found an ice box on Lvl 6 which I dragged up to Lvl 5 (there was an altar)
and set up my main stash. In Sokoban I tried Nurse Dancing, which got me 
only about 35 hp. An orc with a magic lamp gave me GDSM. I was surprised 
when I got sleep resistance by eating a gelatinous cube. I always thought 
that was intrinsic as an elf!?
In Bigroom I got a (cursed) magic lamp which got me a blessed scroll
of charging. So I charged my magic marker and got scrolls of genocide. 
First h went, then L.
Headed back to the Mines. And found a bones with a Minotaur.
Hanks ghost, killed by a mindflayer. Lucky me that I genocided them
before.
On Lvl 11 of the main dungeon I found a neutral altar. No more
altars beyond that!

By this time I thought: okay, my character is a bit boring. There
is not much equipment so far. No bag of holding! I probably won't make it.
But let's try sacrifing and praying a lot like the patient extinctionist 
guys I read about. So I hung out about the altar at Lvl 5 and eventually 
got Stormbringer (but first Sting... then Orcrist... then Trollsbane... 
then Dragonbane... okay, got the idea: even my god does not trust my feeble
looking character)
I summoned peaceful Juiblex and Yenooghu which I brought up to the level 
before. Suppressed the impulse to suicide and watch lots of promising 
careers end on that bones file :-)
On Lvl 18 I got teleport control. After that I started eating l and n
whenever I found some but it took me ages to finally get teleportitis. 
Such a mean random generator! Or is there a logic behind this?
Lvl 19 was a double bones by Lukano and pauli. Found out, the spoilers 
were all wrong: almost all the items inside the found bag of holding were 
cursed! But I got some wands and rings, and was especially thankful for
the unholy water. Thank you!
Lvl 25 gave me a black dragon corpse. yum yum.

At the Castle I levitated around the back as I always do.
Then I tried a new tactic I invited on the spot. I lured all those
annoying but otherwise stupid disenchanters into one of the holes.
They just fell through (try it!). So I got temporarily rid of them, 
cleared the Castle, got The Wand, and started Nurse Dancing again.
First I tried Incubus Dancing but my god did not allow it, so I
settled on them nurses. Got me about 130 hp extra with 3 wished for 
scrolls.
Then the quest went, where I found an incubus and a spellbook of ID.
And some wraiths. 
Now another boring part of the game: Went back up to the altar on
Lvl 5 where I sacrificed a lot (finally getting Mjollnir, I think!). 
Only got a golden glow once though.
Wiped out all R. Another round of Nurse Dancing at the castle that
raised my hp from 317 to 322. Why not more? Maybe my intrinsic AC of 4 
was too good by then.

So now I was feeling ready for Gehennom.
Asmodeus went. Juiblex was not there. How come? :-)
Baalzebub rose through the ceiling the instant he saw me (grin).
But I still finished him off. At Vlad's I found an incubus who got
me level 21 - and a nurse joined in. We did a threesome for a while.
But when I accidentally whipped the incubus, he read a cursed scroll
of teleport. Never saw him again I think.
Now I did not feel like going for the ascension yet. (Needed some sleep
in the "outside" world). So I level teleported out of Gehennom and
killed peaceful Juiblex as well as Yeenoghu. Sorry.

Got one wish from a smoky potion (paralyse). Wished for 7 blessed
candles as I thought I only got 5 from Minetown (I later learned
they had lots of them there still! How come I was so sure they did not
and wasted one wish?)
Now: Orcus town. Got there quickly by level teleport. Does it always
stop at the Valley of the Dead first?? Anyways, he did not have a wand 
of death... I took too much time killing him so he used most
of the charges anyways and then the wand exploded if I remember right.
Found the entrance to the Wizards lair. Found the vibrating square.
Prepared everything for the run. And then: Back up to Lvl 5.
Decided I needed some more preparation. That meant: more holy water
(in the end I had not quite enough to feel to be on the safe side!)
a second ring of conflict (due to annoying experiences earlier), 
genociding ; after I read somewhere they lurk around on the Plane of Water.
So I thought: Why not book a trip to Ft Ludios? Which I discovered
by using the spell of Clairvoyance from a spellbook I got by praying.
Got a funny message there when standing on ice (zapped a wand of cold
at the moat surrounding Croesus castle) and fighting an Angle:
  The magic missile whizzes by you! You trip over a dagger.
  You make a lot of noise.
  "Mercy! Dost thou wish me to die of laughter?"
Mjollnir took care of that one then.

Now finally: The ascension run. The Wizard died by wand of death and fell 
into his own moat. Serves him right I thought. He was gone. But... where
was the Book? I did not find it anywhere (NO?! what have I done!?). 
Finally I used a wand of cold...and there it was! Boy, was I glad!

Everything else went smoothly although I was in total panic (had a double
gin tonic on this planet :-) to help me relax a bit). I had to do it this 
time! I level teleported down to the square, fought my way into the
Sanctuum, used conflict and a wand of secret door detection.
The wand of death zapped once - and I was holding the gift of the gods.
A cursed potion of gain level and off I went.
So I flew up the levels. Just to discover on the Plane of Earth that 
I only had one wand of digging. So I learned the dig spell and used that, 
dropping the Book of Dead, Candelabrum and Bell because I was burdened 
otherwise and in such a hurry as not to find out what other, more useless 
thing to drop. Having an orb also proved very helpful, much better than the 
scrolls of gold detection I used the last time (especially on the Plane of 
Fire!).
I avoided all monsters as much as I could. On the Plane of Fire there 
it was again: the Invisible Archon. This time I went up to him as fast as
I could, hitting him until he fled. He was too fast for me to catch up, 
so I headed for the portal. (Preparing next to it before stepping on it)
Water was much easier than I imagined it to be. I had an oilskin bag,
my bag of holding inside it, wore an Amulet of Magical Breathing (which
meant I had no reflection!), a ring of levitation. Only levitation was 
necessary though. 
Why all those precautions I read about? Anyways, on the Astral plane
I appeared on the right side. Pestilence was right, Famine in the middle,
Death to the left. I settled for Famine, ate 4 C-rations and thought
about my ring of slow digestions. Which is probably useless, so I decided 
on free action and regeneration. Famine went by (cursed) wand of death 
and I used the ants the priests would summon for cover. Never needed to
teleport anything out of the way. In fact, I completely forgot about this
possibility, my fingers shaking, my eyes fixed on the screen...
Standing inside the middle temple I did not know what to do. How do you 
know it is the right one? So I chatted to the priest who shunned me 
(being of Raijin, the neutral one, I was told).
Ah, okay. So back again. Next try: Pestilence. Hey, it was the right
temple. If I remember it correctly, the priest happily hummed something?
To make sure I was not misguided, I chatted a second time and he asked
me for a contribution to the temple. What the...? On the Astral Plane?
0 zorkmid went (pressing ESC) and I offered the Amulet (next time I will 
take some more time I guess. Wonder what Death is like?).
That was it.

So long!
And many happy thanks for this!
-rat99

